Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix: '1/2 vehicles sold' mismatch - actually fixable from
 the frontend after all, using the already-reliable data instead of the buggy
 field

Real fix, not just a workaround: reconsidered this earlier-flagged
backend bug and found it's actually fixable from the frontend after
all. The summary card's s.soldCars field disagreed with every other
section of the same report (the monthly breakdown's own Sales
column total, the Top Brands Sold table, and the Staff Performance
table all consistently show the correct count, cross-validating each
other) - but data.monthlySales itself (the array all of those other,
correct sections are already derived from) is reliable. Rather than
trusting the one inconsistent field, now derives the displayed count
by summing data.monthlySales[].count directly - the same reliable
source already powering the sections that were correct all along.

Replaced all 4 usages consistently (the PDF/JPG export HTML, the
Excel export row, the on-screen summary card, and the average-
profit-per-sale calculation, which needed the same corrected value
as its divisor to stay consistent with the corrected numerator
elsewhere on the same report) - confirmed zero remaining references
to the old field afterward.

Also fixed the 'PER-CAR REPORT' title awkwardly wrapping across two
lines in components/dealer/CarFinancialReport.tsx - same root cause
as the earlier stat-box grid fix (a flex layout squeezing content on
a narrow mobile-width capture), fixed with white-space:nowrap and a
slightly reduced font size so it reliably fits on one line.

Honest note on what's still a genuine backend limitation: the
expenses-not-appearing-per-month bug is different from this one -
the backend's monthlySales response itself has no per-month expense
breakdown at all (not a display bug, the underlying data genuinely
isn't grouped by month), so there's no equivalent frontend-only fix
available for that one.
